{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MagicABindingFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MagicABindingFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.two_regime_dispatch_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.two_regime_dispatch_exists","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L278-L283","doc":"**Two-regime binding dispatcher (existence).** Retained for the\n`prop:magic-A-binding-formula` Lean ref: the doubly-magic regime\nis non-trivially inhabited at the lightest scale (⁴He). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.he4_binding_via_dispatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.he4_binding_via_dispatch","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L264-L276","doc":"**⁴He binding goes through the magic-A formula.** Composing the\ndispatcher with the §3b-cond `MagicABindingFormula` class: when\nthe doubly-magic evaluator is the class binding `B` and `(Z, N)`\nis doubly magic, the dispatched value equals the closed form\n`ρ_F · m_e · A · 8G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingDispatch_alphaShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingDispatch_alphaShift","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L256-L262","doc":"On a non-doubly-magic nucleus the dispatcher returns the α_shift\nevaluator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingDispatch_doublyMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingDispatch_doublyMagic","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L248-L254","doc":"On a doubly-magic nucleus the dispatcher returns the doubly-magic\nevaluator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingDispatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingDispatch","kind":"def","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L230-L246","doc":"**Regime-aware binding evaluator.**\n\nThe single entry point for light-nucleus binding: given a nucleus\n`(Z, N)`, a doubly-magic evaluator `B_dm` (closed-form `8G · A`\nvia `MagicABindingFormula`) and an α_shift evaluator `B_as`\n(per-rep Reeb phase via `BindingForceCarrierKnot`), select the\ncorrect evaluator by the regime classifier.\n\nThis is the operational dispatcher (PR #1543 fix-option 2): ⁴He\nroutes through `B_dm`, non-magic A = 2, 3 candidates route through\n`B_as`. The two underlying evaluators are the §3b-cond\nrigorous-conditional theorems in their respective files; this\nfunction only chooses between them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_dispatches_to_alpha_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_dispatches_to_alpha_shift","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L221-L228","doc":"**Deuteron dispatches to the α_shift regime.** `D = (Z, N) = (1, 1)`:\nneither is magic, so `bindingRegime 1 1 = AlphaShift`; routed\nthrough `BindingForceCarrierKnot` (the `T(2, 3)` trefoil candidate,\n`α_shift = 3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_dispatches_to_alpha_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium3_dispatches_to_alpha_shift","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L213-L219","doc":"**³He dispatches to the α_shift regime.** `³He = (Z, N) = (2, 1)`:\n`N = 1 ∉ 𝔐`, so `bindingRegime 2 1 = AlphaShift`; routed through\n`BindingForceCarrierKnot` (the mirror `T(2, 5)` candidate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tritium_dispatches_to_alpha_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tritium_dispatches_to_alpha_shift","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L204-L211","doc":"**Tritium dispatches to the α_shift regime.** `³H = (Z, N) = (1, 2)`:\n`Z = 1 ∉ 𝔐`, so `bindingRegime 1 2 = AlphaShift`; the binding is\nevaluated through `BindingForceCarrierKnot` (the `T(2, 5)`\ncandidate, `α_shift = 5`, in `binding-alpha-shift-extension.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.he4_dispatches_to_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.he4_dispatches_to_magic","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L196-L202","doc":"**⁴He dispatches to the doubly-magic regime.** `Z = N = 2` are\nboth magic, so `bindingRegime 2 2 = DoublyMagic`; the binding is\nevaluated through `MagicABindingFormula` (this file), giving the\n80× gap closure (`B ≈ 29.956 MeV` vs `28.296 MeV`, 5.9% miss). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingRegime_alphaShift_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingRegime_alphaShift_iff","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L184-L194","doc":"The classifier selects `AlphaShift` exactly when the nucleus is\n*not* doubly magic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingRegime_doublyMagic_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingRegime_doublyMagic_iff","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L172-L182","doc":"The classifier selects `DoublyMagic` exactly on doubly-magic\ninputs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingRegime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingRegime","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L164-L170","doc":"**Regime classifier.** Routes a nucleus `(Z, N)` to its binding\nregime: `DoublyMagic` when both `Z` and `N` are magic, else\n`AlphaShift`. `isMagic` is decidable (finite disjunction of\nequalities), so the dispatch is a total computable function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprBindingRegime.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprBindingRegime.repr","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L162-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instReprBindingRegime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instReprBindingRegime","kind":"instance","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L162-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqBindingRegime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableEqBindingRegime","kind":"instance","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L162-L162","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingRegime.DoublyMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingRegime.DoublyMagic","kind":"ctor","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L160-L161","doc":"Doubly-magic regime (Borromean residue `8G · A`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingRegime.AlphaShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingRegime.AlphaShift","kind":"ctor","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L158-L159","doc":"Single-hyperbolic-knot regime (per-rep Reeb phase, `T(p, k)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BindingRegime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BindingRegime","kind":"inductive","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L140-L162","doc":"**Binding regime tag.**\n\nThe light-nucleus binding evaluator is the disjoint union of two\ncategorical regimes. A nucleus `(Z, N)` is routed to exactly one:\n\n- `DoublyMagic` — both `Z, N ∈ 𝔐`. The Littlewood–Richardson\n  fusion of the Z-block and N-block collapses to a single\n  self-conjugate Specht module\n  (`conj:diagrammatic-double-magic-lr-fusion`); there is no\n  Wedderburn channel, no hyperbolic force-carrier knot, no per-rep\n  Reeb phase. Binding is set by the universal Borromean residue\n  `8G` scaled by nucleon count via `MagicABindingFormula`.\n- `AlphaShift` — at least one of `Z, N ∉ 𝔐`. The nucleus carries a\n  single hyperbolic force-carrier torus knot `T(p, k)` whose\n  per-rep Reeb phase `α_shift = k·(p−1)` sets the binding via\n  `BindingForceCarrierKnot`\n  (`prop:binding-alpha-shift-extension`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.he4_is_doubly_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.he4_is_doubly_magic","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L129-L138","doc":"**⁴He instance** of the doubly-magic regime.\n\nZ = N = 2 are both magic; the witness compute\n(`magic_A_formula.py::magic_A_binding(2, 2)`) gives `ρ_F = 2`\nyielding B ≈ 29.956 MeV vs experimental 28.296 MeV (5.9% miss).\n\nThis existence theorem confirms the doubly-magic predicate\nis non-trivially inhabited at the lightest scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.magic_A_binding_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.magic_A_binding_formula","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L116-L127","doc":"**Magic-A binding theorem** (rigorous-conditional per §3b-cond).\n\nFor any doubly-magic (Z, N), the binding equals\n`ρ_F · m_e · A · 8G` where `A = Z + N`. Sorry-free conditional\non the `MagicABindingFormula` class hypothesis. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:magic-A-binding-formula","label":"prop:magic-A-binding-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula.formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula.formula","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The doubly-magic binding formula: B(Z, N) = ρ_F · m_e · A · 8G. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula.rho_F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula.rho_F","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The substrate-determined prefactor for the (Z, N) regime.\n⁴He uses `rho_F = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MagicABindingFormula","kind":"class","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L78-L114","doc":"**Doubly-magic binding formula class** (§3b-cond hypothesis).\n\nAxiomatises the substrate-determined prefactor `ρ_F` and the\nformula `B(Z, N) = ρ_F · m_e · A · 8G` for doubly-magic (Z, N).\nThe class field `formula` records the binding evaluation.\n\nReanalysis (2026-05-31, see audit\n`docs/audits/2026-05-31-binding-magic-A-wireup.md`): the\nderivation of `ρ_F` was previously framed here as Open Math A,\nbut is structurally answered by\n`conj:kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity` (RESOLVED\n2026-05-24, Rule-14 owner-authorised): `ρ_F = ν_SDP` (joint-\ntower SDP Wedderburn multiplicity), driver (x) of the canonical\n13-menu. The class hypothesis below can be replaced (Sprint 2)\nwith a derivation from the SDP-multiplicity Lean class once it\nis in place. Only the numerical verification\n`ν_SDP(⁴He) = 2` (joint-tower SDP solver extension) remains\nopen; structural derivation is closed.\n\nRemaining R&D follow-up:\n1. Extend joint-tower SDP solver to confirm `ν_SDP(⁴He) = 2`\n   (currently extrapolated from the SDP-confirmed D, T, ³He\n   census).\n2. Extend to higher-A doubly-magic candidates (¹⁶O Z=N=8,\n   ⁴⁰Ca Z=N=20) by computing each `ν_SDP` via the same SDP\n   infrastructure.\n\nThe class hypothesis is sorry-free per §3b-cond: any instance\ndischarges `formula` definitionally for its specific (Z, N). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CatalanPrefactor.vol_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CatalanPrefactor.vol_borromean","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The value of `8G` in the given coefficient ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CatalanPrefactor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CatalanPrefactor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CatalanPrefactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CatalanPrefactor","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L68-L76","doc":"Borromean residue prefactor `8G = Vol(L6a4)`, where G is\nCatalan's constant. Approximate value 7.32772475... (mpmath\n50dps). The exact value is delivered by\n`prop:gravity-spectral-prefactor`; here we abstract it as a\nparameter so the formula statement does not depend on the\nCatalan-constant Mathlib import depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.isDoublyMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.isDoublyMagic","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L62-L66","doc":"A light nucleus (Z, N) is *doubly magic* if both Z and N lie in\nthe magic-number set. The canonical doubly-magic light example\nis ⁴He with Z = N = 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableIsMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.instDecidableIsMagic","kind":"instance","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L57-L60","doc":"`isMagic` is decidable: a finite disjunction of decidable\nequalities on `ℕ`. Needed for the `bindingRegime` dispatch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.isMagic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.isMagic","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/magic-A-binding-formula.lean#L50-L55","doc":"The set of magic numbers {2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}. Mirrors\n`QOU.Common.magicSet` (single source of truth referenced from\n`magic-numbers-bring.lean`). Inlined here to keep this file\nstandalone for the sibling-trace convention. ","signatureChunk":0}]}